      "id": 1,
      "text": "Spangler emerged in 1893 when bituminous coal mining became the dominant industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spangler%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s economy was driven by coal companies like Madeira-Hill and Springfield, plus lumber, a shirt factory, and a local brewery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Spangler,_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1909 a Miners' Hospital opened to treat injured coal workers, later expanded in 1919 under labor leader John Brophy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Spangler,_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Immigrant labor from Eastern Europe—Slovaks, Poles, and others—shaped Spangler’s workforce during its mining boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Spangler,_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The West Branch Susquehanna River enabled early loggers to float timber downstream, supporting the region’s first timber industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Spangler,_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Cheryl Strayed, author of Wild, was born in Spangler and later portrayed by Reese Witherspoon in the film.",
